# The settings of a Chaos Gateway installation. Docker Compose reads them from the file .env next to compose.yaml (the host setup,
# deploy/host-setup.sh --image, writes the first two); every line below is optional and shows its default.

# The image and its version. update.sh --version V changes the version.
#CHAOSGW_IMAGE=ghcr.io/andste82/chaos-gateway
#CHAOSGW_VERSION=latest

# The port of the web UI and the API (HTTPS) as the setup configured it (8443 unless you chose another). The services of the
# gateway (DNS proxy, TLS responder, Kea's hook), the health check of the API container and update.sh reach the API on it: set it
# here when you changed the port, or the API container is reported unhealthy.
#CHAOSGW_UI_PORT=8443

# Optional containers: the interception proxy (plan §2.8; mitmproxy, not validated on ARM64 hardware).
#COMPOSE_PROFILES=interception
# A file of CA certificates that the proxy trusts for the servers it connects to (a path inside the container, which you mount
# with a compose file of your own, docs/install.md), or no check of the servers' certificates at all.
#CHAOSGW_UPSTREAM_CA_FILE=
#CHAOSGW_UPSTREAM_INSECURE=0
